    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "To prepare the samples, 0.1 g of mycelium was ground in liquid nitrogen. Each sample was then mixed with four volumes of phenol extraction buffer (containing 10 mM DTT and 1% protease inhibitor) and subjected to ultrasonic disruption. Equal volumes of Tris-equilibrated phenol were added, and the mixture was centrifuged at 5,500 g for 10 min at 4 °C. The supernatant was collected and precipitated overnight by adding five volumes of 0.1 M ammonium acetate/methanol. The resulting precipitate was washed sequentially with methanol and acetone. For enzymatic digestion, equal amounts of protein from each sample were taken and mixed with one volume of pre-chilled acetone, vortexed, and then an additional four volumes of pre-chilled acetone were added. The mixture was incubated at -20 °C for 2 hours. Following this, the samples were centrifuged at 4,500 g for 5 min, and the supernatant was discarded. The precipitate was washed twice with pre-chilled acetone and then allowed to dry. The dried precipitate was resuspended in TEAB to a final concentration of 200 mM and sonicated to dissolve. Trypsin was added, and the samples were digested overnight. Subsequently, DTT was added to achieve a final concentration of 5 mM, and the samples were reduced at 56 °C for 30 min. After reduction, iodoacetamide (IAM, Sigma-Aldrich) was added to a final concentration of 11 mM, and the reaction was incubated in the dark at room temperature for 15 min. The resulting peptides were dissolved in mobile phase A for liquid chromatography and separated using a NanoElute ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography (UHPLC) system. Following separation, the peptides were injected into a capillary ion source for ionization and subsequently analyzed by timsTOF Pro mass spectrometry.",
